            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a fork, then the Persian for to cross."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: جهت",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جهت (jahat) — \"a direction; a side\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ما در جهت اشتباه رانندگی میکردیم. Mâ dar jahat-e eshtebâh rânandegi mikardim. We were driving in the wrong direction."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic plural jahât. Be in jahat — for this reason."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jahat was borrowed from Arabic and is usually traced to Arabic jiha 'side, direction'. EtymDB does not list it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
