          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قطب نما (qotbnamâ) — \"a compass\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در کوه با قطب نما راه را پیدا کردیم. Dar kuh bâ qotbnamâ râh râ peydâ kardim. In the mountains we found the way with a compass."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally 'pole-shower': qotb 'pole' + namâ 'showing'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "qotbnamâ is built from qotb 'pole', borrowed from Arabic quṭb (EtymDB lists the Arabic word), and native namâ 'showing', the stem of nemudan 'to show'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
